<title>ITALY: OLYMPICS-HAVELANGE TIPS EUROPE TO HOST 2004 GAMES.</title>
<headline>OLYMPICS-HAVELANGE TIPS EUROPE TO HOST 2004 GAMES.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>FIFA president Joao Havelange said on Tuesday he expected a European country to win the race for the 2004 Olympics.</p>
<p>Havelange, who is also a member of the IOC, was in Rome to examine the city's bid to be chosen from among a short-list which also includes Athens, Stockholm, Cape Town and Buenos Aires.</p>
<p>&quot;The south of the world, and particularly South America, are pushing Buenos Aires but it will be the 111 members of the IOC who decide and of these almost half are European,&quot; Havelange said.</p>
<p>&quot;Is there any need for me to go on?&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
